`]}),e.jsxs(n,{title:"Later versions keep the function and change the kernel",children:[e.jsx(t.p,{children:"FA1 and its successors compute the same mathematical attention function with the same three ideas. What changes from one version to the next is the kernel, which follows the hardware resource that binds on a newer GPU generation."}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["FA2, on A100-era hardware, partitions the work better and spends less time on operations other than matrix multiplications ",e.jsx(a,{id:"dao2024fa2",children:"Dao, 2024"}),". FlashAttention-3 (FA3) targets Hopper GPUs such as the H100. It uses Hopper's asynchronous execution to overlap data movement with computation ",e.jsx(a,{id:"shah2024",children:"Shah et al., 2024"}),". FlashAttention-4 (FA4) targets Blackwell. It rebalances the work among three units: the Tensor Cores, the special-function units (SFUs), which evaluate functions such as the exponential, and shared memory ",e.jsx(a,{id:"zadouri2026",children:"Zadouri et al., 2026"}),"."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(i,{title:"Gated attention",optional:!0,accent:2,number:"46",children:[e.jsx(s,{math:"\\tilde o_{t,h}=o_{t,h}\\odot\\sigma(W^G_h h_t),\\qquad u_t=W_O[\\tilde o_{t,1};\\dots;\\tilde o_{t,H}]",label:"gated attention output"}),e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
